  "description": "Details of condition 9 'Bat boxes/bricks' pursuant to planning permission 23/AP/1993 'The proposed development includes the refurbishment of Consort Park and Dr Harold Moody Park, including connecting the two parks together by closing the eastern end of Sturdy Road to motor traffic, and transforming this section of highway into park land. Works to Consort Park include reduction and remodelling of existing mounds, tree removals, new footpaths, seating, creation of meadows, tiny forest and specimens tree planting. Works to Dr Harold Moody Park include expansion and refurbishment of existing playground, amendments to multi-use games court fencing, new pump track, miscellaneous informal sports equipment and cycle parking. Tree planting, hedging and planting. Closure of the existing pedestrian entrance to Dr Harold Moody Park from Gordon Road to facilitate expansion of the playground. Works to the stopped up section of Sturdy Road includes earthworks, new footpath link to Gordon Road, tree planting and turning head within Dr Harold Moody Park.'",
